# The host build tree must never enter the image: it holds macOS/arm64 objects
# and a vcpkg_installed/ built for the host triplet. Copying it in would both
# bloat the context by gigabytes and risk CMake reusing host artifacts.
# Both spellings: the presets in CMakePresets.json create build_asan/ and
# build_tsan/ with UNDERSCORES, and only the hyphenated names were listed here
# - so the two sanitizer trees (gigabytes of host objects) were being sent to
# the daemon on every build. They never entered the image, because the
# Dockerfile copies named source directories only, but they cost context
# transfer time - and the test stages below now create identically named
# directories INSIDE the image, where a host copy would be actively harmful.
build/
build-debug/
build_debug/
build-asan/
build_asan/
build-tsan/
build_tsan/
build-bench/
cmake-build-*/
out/
vcpkg_installed/

# CMake scratch
CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles/
CMakePresets.json
cmake_install.cmake
compile_commands.json
CTestTestfile.cmake
.cmake/
.cache/

# Docs and VCS - not needed to compile, and they change often enough to
# invalidate layers for no reason.
.git/
.github/
docs/
*.md

# Editor / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
*.swp

# Build outputs
*.o
*.a
*.so
*.dylib
